# Code owners are automatically requested as reviewers when someone opens a pull request
# that touches a matching path. For this to have teeth, Settings -> Rulesets (or branch
# protection) must require review before merging on the protected branches.
#
# Security-related files, as recommended by GitHub:
.github/
# Build and release tooling:
*.java
*.xml
*.gradle
*.toml
*.yml
*.yaml
# Anything else that is not covered by a later rule:
*

# --- Tamper-sensitive assets -------------------------------------------------
# Donation QR codes. Replacing one would redirect donations to whoever submitted
# the change, so these require the maintainer's approval explicitly.
#
# Without a ruleset requiring review, CODEOWNERS only sends a review request --
# it does not block the merge. Pair this file with that setting.
.github/sponsor/*.png